---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalLayout from '@components/article/LegalLayout.astro';
import { buildCategorySchema, buildMeta } from '@lib/seo';
import { analyticsEnv } from '@lib/analytics-env';

// The DevTeam sink exists only on a configured preview build; the live site
// reports to Google Analytics alone. Named here so the processor list below
// states exactly what this build sends, rather than what some build might.
const devteamSink = analyticsEnv().key !== '';

const meta = buildMeta({
  title: 'Privacy policy',
  description:
    'How SleekDrops handles your data: anonymous analytics you can switch off, advertising consent handled by our advertising partner, minimal first-party storage, affiliate disclosure, and no sale of personal data.',
  pathname: '/privacy',
});
---
<BaseLayout
  {...meta}
  schema={buildCategorySchema('Privacy policy', '/privacy', meta.description)}
  screen="privacy"
>
  <LegalLayout
    eyebrow="Legal"
    titleHtml="Privacy <em>policy</em>."
    updated="September 28, 2026"
    toc={[
      { href: '#summary',      label: 'Plain summary' },
      { href: '#scope',        label: 'Scope of this policy' },
      { href: '#data',         label: 'What we collect' },
      { href: '#how-we-use',   label: 'How we use it' },
      { href: '#cookies',      label: 'Cookies & tracking' },
      { href: '#affiliate',    label: 'Affiliate disclosure' },
      { href: '#ads',          label: 'Advertising partners' },
      { href: '#third-parties', label: 'Third-party services' },
      { href: '#retention',    label: 'Data retention' },
      { href: '#security',     label: 'Security' },
      { href: '#children',     label: "Children's privacy" },
      { href: '#rights-gdpr',  label: 'EU/UK rights (GDPR)' },
      { href: '#rights-ca',    label: 'California rights (CCPA)' },
      { href: '#do-not-sell',  label: 'Do Not Sell or Share' },
      { href: '#changes',      label: 'Changes to this policy' },
      { href: '#contact',      label: 'Contact us' },
    ]}
  >
    <div class="summary" id="summary">
      <strong>Plain summary</strong>
      We host on Cloudflare and keep browser storage to a minimum. Anonymous, aggregate analytics is on by default, and you can switch it off at any time under <strong>Privacy preferences</strong> in the footer. Our advertising partner, Mediavine, manages advertising consent through its own consent notice where the law requires one. Most outbound product links are affiliate links, which may earn us a small commission at no extra cost to you.
    </div>

    <h2 id="scope">Scope of this <em>policy</em></h2>
    <p>This policy explains how SleekDrops ("we," "us," "our") collects, uses, discloses, and protects information when you visit <strong>sleekdrops.com</strong> or any subdomain we operate, or contact us by email. It does not cover third-party websites we link to — once you click an outbound link, the destination's privacy policy governs your interaction with them.</p>
    <p><strong>Data controller:</strong> SleekDrops, an independently operated Australian digital publication. Contact <a href="mailto:privacy@sleekdrops.com">privacy@sleekdrops.com</a> for privacy rights, complaints or data requests.</p>

    <h2 id="data">What we <em>collect</em></h2>
    <p>SleekDrops is a static publication. The site itself stores no personal data about you directly. The following limited information is collected by services we rely on:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Server logs.</strong> Our host (Cloudflare) automatically logs IP addresses, user-agent strings, and request paths for security, abuse prevention, and performance — standard for any website. We do not access or analyse these logs.</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics.</strong> Anonymous analytics is on by default. We record aggregate events such as page views, outbound clicks, reading completion and use of page controls, together with limited context such as the page path, category, content slug and placement. We strip personal data in your browser before an event is sent, so names, email addresses, full query strings and typed text are not included. A Global Privacy Control or Do-Not-Track signal keeps analytics off, and you can switch it off at any time under <strong>Privacy preferences</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>Outbound affiliate clicks.</strong> When you follow one of our <code>/go/</code> product links, our server chooses the appropriate retailer destination for your country. It does not store your IP address, browser or a cookie. The redirect carries a freshly generated random reference to the retailer's affiliate network so a later commission can be matched to that click; it is new for every click and is not used to recognise you on this site or another visit.</li>
      <li><strong>Email.</strong> If you write to one of the addresses shown on the site, we receive your email address and whatever information you include in the message.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not collect special-category personal data (health, biometric, political opinions, etc.), and we never knowingly collect data from children — see <a href="#children">Children's privacy</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="how-we-use">How we <em>use it</em></h2>
    <p>We use the limited information described above to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Operate the site, fix bugs, and keep things working;</li>
      <li>Understand which posts are useful (aggregate analytics only);</li>
      <li>Respond to messages sent to our published email addresses;</li>
      <li>Comply with legal obligations and prevent fraud or abuse.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not use your data for automated decision-making, sell it to data brokers or train AI models on it. Our advertising partner may personalise ads only where your consent choices permit it; see <a href="#ads">Advertising partners</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="cookies">Cookies &amp; <em>tracking</em></h2>
    <p>We use cookies and similar technologies, including local and session storage on your device. With analytics switched off we store only two first-party items besides your privacy choice (below), and neither of them is a cookie:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>sd-theme</code> — browser local storage. Remembers your dark-mode preference (kept until you clear your browser).</li>
      <li><code>sd-bookmarks</code> — browser local storage. Stores the article slugs you've saved (kept in your browser only; never sent to us).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We store your analytics choice (<code>sd-consent</code>) in your browser's local storage as an essential setting that never leaves your browser, once you have made one. While analytics is on, three more items are written:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>sd_sid</code> — browser session storage (not a cookie). Groups page views from a single visit so analytics counts sessions correctly. It is randomly generated, is never derived from you or your device, and is used for nothing else. Cleared when the browser tab is closed, and replaced after 30 minutes of inactivity.</li>
      <li>Google Analytics' own first-party measurement cookies (such as <code>_ga</code>), used to count visits.</li>
      <li><code>sd-exp</code> in browser local storage, which records only which version of a page layout or wording you were shown so we can compare them in aggregate.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>These items exist only to make the anonymous analytics countable and are not used for advertising or cross-site tracking. Switching analytics off under <strong>Privacy preferences</strong> deletes <code>sd_sid</code>, <code>sd-exp</code> and Google Analytics' <code>_ga</code> cookies immediately, sends an updated denied signal through Google Consent Mode v2 and stops further measurement.</p>
    <p>Amazon may set its own cookies on <strong>the destination retailer's domain</strong> after you follow an affiliate link. Our advertising partner, Mediavine, sets cookies and similar technologies of its own to serve and measure advertising, and shows a consent notice where the law requires one; what it collects and how to opt out is set out under <a href="#ads">Advertising partners</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="affiliate">Affiliate <em>disclosure</em></h2>
    <p>In accordance with the United States Federal Trade Commission's 16 CFR Part 255 ("Guides Concerning the Use of Endorsements and Testimonials in Advertising"), we disclose the following:</p>
    <blockquote>
      <p>SleekDrops is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program, which provides a means for sites to earn advertising fees by linking to Amazon. As an Amazon Associate, we earn from qualifying purchases.</p>
    </blockquote>
    <p>When you click a product link on SleekDrops and complete a qualifying purchase within the retailer's cookie window, the retailer attributes the sale to us and pays us a small commission. <strong>The price you pay is the same whether you click our link or not</strong> — the retailer absorbs the commission out of their margin. We never see who you are, what you purchased, or your payment details. We only see that an order was attributed to SleekDrops.</p>
    <p>For full details on how we choose what to link to, how we research, and how affiliate links are labelled, see the <a href="/disclaimer">Affiliate disclaimer</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="ads">Advertising <em>partners</em></h2>
    <p>SleekDrops works with <strong>Journey by Mediavine</strong> to serve the display advertising on this site, and with no other programmatic advertising network. Mediavine's own notice follows, reproduced as it requires. The consent notice it describes is shown where the law requires one, and the "Update Privacy Settings" and "Do Not Sell or Share My Information" controls it refers to are added to the foot of the page by Mediavine where they apply.</p>

    <div class="mediavine-privacy-notice">
      <h2>Mediavine Advertising Privacy Notice v. 1.2</h2>

      <p>Mediavine works with this site to support the delivery of ads that align with your interests. It collects information about your online activities and browsing information, including websites you visit, pages you view, search terms, the apps you use, the language and device you use, location, and emails from newsletter sign ups. This information is then passed to partners to enable them to display interest based advertising to you.</p>

      <p>This Notice is specific to Mediavine and explains how Mediavine collects, uses, shares, or sells your personal information when you visit this site or sign up for a newsletter managed by Mediavine. This website must disclose any collection, use, sharing or sale of personal data beyond the services provided by Mediavine in its own privacy notice (above) and comply with relevant privacy laws.</p>

      <h3>What personal data does Mediavine collect?</h3>
      <p>Mediavine may collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>IP Address (unique address that identifies your computer or phone on the internet)</li>
        <li>Location (country, city, state)</li>
        <li>Operating System (e.g., Windows or Mac)</li>
        <li>Device Information (hardware, platform, location and carrier data)</li>
        <li>Language of the Website or Browser</li>
        <li>Web Browser Type (e.g., Chrome, Firefox or Safari)</li>
        <li>Email address</li>
      </ul>

      <p>When you visit this site, Mediavine uses cookies and similar technologies, such as pixels and tags, to collect your information about your behavior on this site and other websites you visit, across your devices. These tools track preferences, website visits and activities, interactions with emails and ads, and evaluate effectiveness of emails and ads and record which ads have been shown to you to enable the delivery of interest based ads on this site. To learn more, please visit <a href="https://www.allaboutcookies.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">allaboutcookies.org</a>; <a href="https://ico.org.uk/for-the-public/online/cookies/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ICO - What are cookies and similar technologies</a>; <a href="https://learnwebanalytics.com/whats-the-difference-between-a-cookie-a-pixel-and-a-tag" target="_blank" rel="noopener">learnwebanalytics.com</a>.</p>

      <p>In some cases, Mediavine may manage a site's newsletter. Mediavine collects your email directly from you through the newsletter sign up form, and will request your consent to use your email for interest based advertising. Your email will be converted into hashed format – a unique set of numbers and letters representing your email – before being sent to partners. If you no longer wish to receive this newsletter, you may unsubscribe at any time using the "Unsubscribe" button.</p>

      <h3>Does Mediavine share or sell my personal information for interest based advertising?</h3>
      <p>Yes, Mediavine will use, share, license, sell or otherwise disclose your personal information to our partners to enable interest based advertising to be displayed to you on this site. Through the bidstream, an online marketplace, Mediavine shares data, such as ad location, site content, and your personal information with advertisers. Using this information, advertisers bid for ad space, and the winning bidder gets to display their ad to you on this site.</p>

      <p>Mediavine may share your personal data with partners to create a universal (unique) identifier linked to your online behavior and preferences. This identifier is added to the bid request to improve the targeting of interest based ads. Mediavine and its partners may also combine your personal data collected from your interaction with this site with your data that they have collected from other sources to create a profile of your interests and behaviors to provide interest based advertising across your online experience, including devices, browsers, and applications. Mediavine could also license your personal data from its partners to enrich the information in its bid request to advertisers.</p>

      <p>To learn more about Mediavine partners, visit <a href="https://www.mediavine.com/ad-partners" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mediavine.com/ad-partners</a>.</p>

      <h3>How can I opt out of interest based advertising?</h3>
      <p>To opt out of interest based advertising on this site, you may take the following actions:</p>

      <h4>Cookie Consent – For EU/UK visitors</h4>
      <p>On first visit to the site, you may reject the use of cookies through the cookie consent banner, shown only where legally required. If you initially accept the use of cookies, but change your mind, you can access the banner by clicking "Update Privacy Settings" at the bottom of the home page to change your preferences at any time.</p>

      <h4>Disabling Cookies</h4>
      <p>To learn more about cookies and how to disable them for interest based advertising, visit <a href="https://www.allaboutcookies.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">All About Cookies</a>. Most browsers provide options in their menu to stop accepting new cookies, alert you to new cookies, disable cookies, and clear your browser's cache or storage. Be aware that blocking cookies may affect your site experience, and essential cookies cannot be disabled as these are necessary for the website to function.</p>

      <h4>Opting Out Using Other Tools</h4>
      <p>Use the following tools to opt out of receiving interest-based advertising:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Digital Advertising Alliance (DAA) WebChoice Tool: <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener">optout.aboutads.info</a></li>
        <li>Network Advertising Initiative (NAI): <a href="https://thenai.org/opt-out" target="_blank" rel="noopener">thenai.org/opt-out</a></li>
        <li>Ad Choices (EDAA): <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">youronlinechoices.com</a></li>
        <li>Ad Choices (DAAC): <a href="https://youradchoices.ca/en/tools" target="_blank" rel="noopener">youradchoices.ca/en/tools</a></li>
        <li>AppChoices (Mobile Device): <a href="https://youradchoices.ca/en/tools" target="_blank" rel="noopener">youradchoices.ca/en/tools</a></li>
        <li>Global Privacy Control (GPC): <a href="https://globalprivacycontrol.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">globalprivacycontrol.org</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h4>Opt-Out Rights in Certain US States</h4>
      <p>If you reside in certain US states, you have the right to opt out of the sale or sharing of your personal data. A "Do Not Sell or Share My Information" button can be found at the bottom of the home page, where required.</p>

      <h4>Seeing Ads After Opting Out or Disabling Ads</h4>
      <p>Disabling cookies or opting out of the sales or sharing of personal data for advertising does not mean you won't see ads on this website. It means the ads you see will not be personalized to your online behavior and interests.</p>

      <h3>What are my data protection rights?</h3>
      <p>Under data protection laws in the EU, UK and certain US states, you may have the right to delete, access, request a copy, and correct your personal information. If you'd like to exercise these rights related to the services we provide to this website, please contact Mediavine at <a href="mailto:privacy@mediavine.com">privacy@mediavine.com</a>.</p>

      <h3>Will Mediavine transfer my personal data to the US?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Mediavine transfers your data to the US for processing and storage. To safeguard this transfer, Mediavine enters into agreements known as Standard Contractual Clauses with our vendors and partners to ensure your data is protected according to EU or UK privacy standards.</p>

      <h3>How does Mediavine protect my personal information?</h3>
      <p>Mediavine has implemented technical and organizational security measures appropriate to the risk to the personal data. Despite our safeguards and efforts, no internet transmission can be 100% secure.</p>

      <h3>How long does Mediavine keep my personal information?</h3>
      <p>Where Mediavine processes personal data to enable interest based advertising, we will continue to process until you ask us to stop.</p>

      <h3>How can I contact Mediavine if I have questions about this notice or its services to this website?</h3>
      <p>Please contact us at <a href="mailto:Privacy@mediavine.com">Privacy@mediavine.com</a>, or you may write to us at: 159 W. 25th St., Suite #427, New York, NY 10001.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 id="third-parties">Third-party <em>services</em></h2>
    <p>The following services may process limited data on our behalf:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> (USA / global) — hosting, CDN, security. Privacy policy: <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">cloudflare.com/privacypolicy</a>.</li>
      {devteamSink && <li><strong>DevTeam Analytics</strong> - anonymous product analytics for the non-production preview. The live sleekdrops.com build blocks this sink.</li>}
      <li><strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> (USA / global) — aggregate traffic measurement, on by default and switched off under <strong>Privacy preferences</strong>. We send page paths rather than full URLs so query strings never reach Google. Privacy policy: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Amazon Associates</strong> — an affiliate network and independent controller that may receive limited information, such as a referring URL and cookie ID, after you follow an affiliate link to Amazon.</li>
      <li><strong>Mediavine</strong> (USA / global) — our advertising partner, which serves and measures the display advertising on this site and is an independent controller of what it collects; see <a href="#ads">Advertising partners</a> for its notice, its partners and the opt-out tools it provides.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="retention">Data <em>retention</em></h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Email messages:</strong> up to 24 months, then deleted.</li>
      <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> retained by Cloudflare per their default retention (typically 7–30 days).</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> aggregate-only data; retained up to 36 months.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
    <p>We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect the limited personal data we hold — HTTPS in transit, encrypted storage at rest with our providers, and access controls on administrative tools. No method of transmission over the Internet is 100% secure; while we strive to use commercially acceptable means, we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

    <h2 id="children">Children's <em>privacy</em></h2>
    <p>SleekDrops is not directed at children under 13 (or under 16 in the EU/UK). We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided us with personal data, contact <a href="mailto:privacy@sleekdrops.com">privacy@sleekdrops.com</a> and we will delete it. This commitment is in line with the Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA) and the UK's Age-Appropriate Design Code.</p>

    <h2 id="rights-gdpr">EU/UK rights <em>(GDPR)</em></h2>
    <p>If you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or Switzerland, you have the following rights with respect to your personal data:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access</strong> — request a copy of any personal data we hold about you, such as an email you sent us.</li>
      <li><strong>Rectification</strong> — ask us to correct inaccurate data.</li>
      <li><strong>Erasure</strong> — ask us to delete your data ("right to be forgotten").</li>
      <li><strong>Restriction</strong> — ask us to limit processing in certain circumstances.</li>
      <li><strong>Portability</strong> — receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format.</li>
      <li><strong>Objection</strong> — object to processing based on legitimate interests, including direct marketing.</li>
      <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time where processing is based on consent, including personalised advertising; analytics can be switched off at any time under <strong>Privacy preferences</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>Lodge a complaint</strong> with your local supervisory authority.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Our legal bases for processing are: <strong>consent</strong> (personalised advertising, where the law requires it), <strong>legitimate interests</strong> (operating the site, aggregate analytics, fraud prevention and responding to email), and <strong>legal obligation</strong> (responding to lawful requests).</p>

    <h2 id="rights-ca">California rights <em>(CCPA / CPRA)</em></h2>
    <p>If you are a California resident, the California Consumer Privacy Act ("CCPA") and California Privacy Rights Act ("CPRA") give you specific rights:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The right to know what personal information we collect, use, disclose, and (if applicable) sell or share.</li>
      <li>The right to delete personal information we have collected from you.</li>
      <li>The right to correct inaccurate personal information.</li>
      <li>The right to opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information.</li>
      <li>The right to limit use and disclosure of sensitive personal information.</li>
      <li>The right to non-discrimination for exercising any of these rights.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell personal information in the traditional sense. See <a href="#do-not-sell">Do Not Sell or Share</a> below for details on what constitutes a "sale" under the CPRA and how to opt out.</p>

    <h2 id="do-not-sell">Do Not Sell or Share My <em>Personal Information</em></h2>
    <p>SleekDrops does not sell your personal information for monetary consideration. Some laws may treat personalised-advertising data as a “share.” You can decline personalised advertising through Mediavine's consent notice where it is shown, through the opt-out tools listed in its notice above, or with a Global Privacy Control signal; and you can switch off our separate analytics category under <strong>Privacy preferences</strong>.</p>
    <p>To opt out of any such sharing, or to exercise any other privacy right, email <a href="mailto:privacy@sleekdrops.com">privacy@sleekdrops.com</a> with the subject line "Privacy Request." We honour the Global Privacy Control (GPC) signal where technically feasible.</p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes to this <em>policy</em></h2>
    <p>We may update this policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or applicable law. When we do, we will update the "Last updated" date at the top of this page. Material changes will be announced on the homepage for at least 14 days.</p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact <em>us</em></h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy, or want your data removed? Email <a href="mailto:privacy@sleekdrops.com">privacy@sleekdrops.com</a>; the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> lists our other addresses. We aim to respond within five working days, and within 30 days for any formal access or deletion request under GDPR or CCPA.</p>
  </LegalLayout>
</BaseLayout>
